% expect-error: limitcheck
% divergence: masked-dct-interleaved
% Scenario: an image interleaved by row with its mask whose data comes
% through DCTDecode cannot be separated from the mask without decoding
% the stream: limitcheck, and nothing is painted. The stream is the
% project's own 16x16 grey baseline JPEG (`cargo xtask tiny-jpeg`),
% so a decoder can read it; its 256 samples fall short of the 288
% bytes the interleaved layout asks for, which cuts the image.
100 100 translate
200 200 scale
%%BeginData: 12 ASCII Lines
<< /ImageType 3 /InterleaveType 2
   /DataDict << /ImageType 1 /Width 16 /Height 16 /BitsPerComponent 8
      /ImageMatrix [16 0 0 -16 0 16] /Decode [0 1]
      /DataSource currentfile /ASCIIHexDecode filter /DCTDecode filter >>
   /MaskDict << /ImageType 1 /Width 16 /Height 16 /BitsPerComponent 1
      /ImageMatrix [16 0 0 -16 0 16] /Decode [0 1] >> >> image
